// Plan stage R0z Z9c-B (R-VREF, review round 2, B3 and B4; the bad twin):
// a reference can be live in the window of the task, so the call keeps the
// rule of main. The probe of the review:
// Review probe Z9c-B r2 (R-VREF edge): `par` gets a reference from the function parameter `get` and gives it
// to its closure `f`, which holds `r` into it while the task of `h` pushes to `w`.
fn par(h: fn(), get: fn() -> &Vec<u64>) / async {
    let v = get()
    let f = |u: &Vec<u64>| { let r = &u[0]; scope { s => s.spawn(h); () }; print(r) }
    f(v)
}
fn main() / async {
    let w = Vec.new()
    w.push(1)
    par(|| w.push(2), || &w)
}
